 tragedy that  has hit nearly every indian  including this one it's a tsunami that  overwhelms the country  every day in case numbers that's more  than 380  000 just in the past 24 hours  relatives trying to arrange oxygen for  their loved ones trying to arrange beds  trying to arrange medical supplies most  of the time  failing in the process  the fires burn day and night  but delhi's morticians are barely able  to keep  up these makeshift crematoriums  have become a symbol of india's kovid 19  catastrophe  this was a parking lot but we got  permission to set up an extra  24 crematorium sites and now there are  so many corpses  we're running out of firewood  [Music]  kovid 19 has taken an enormous toll on  india  many died because there was no one to  take care of them  for days there have been lines of  patients in front of hospitals  no one lets them in because there aren't  enough beds  or oxygen tanks people feel abandoned  and my father is in a very critical  condition i'm getting no help  numbers are given there but nobody is  responding  numbers are not reachable please help me  please  my father is dying i can't afford  another loss i  yesterday i lost my younger brother my  father  my father begged me to help him but i  couldn't do you know how that feels when  your own father cries  and all you can do is put him in an auto  rickshaw without an oxygen tank  for three days i've been walking from  one hospital to the next  i've never seen anything like this in my  life  the doctors are aware of these  catastrophic circumstances  but they can't do anything about it one  hospital director told dw news  the situation is out of control i'm  used to making decisions and getting  them implemented  but i feel so helpless now i get more  than 500 calls every day  from people asking for beds asking for  oxygen asking for help  many people are scared and want to get  vaccinated  but there isn't enough vaccine to go  around  even though india is the world's largest  va